{
  "name": "calendar-update",
  "description": "Events in ics calendars (one with seeded events, one read-only, one holding a daily series) and a storage calendar. listEvents: one calendar, all calendars, table format, maxResults, a weekly series expanded into its occurrences with one changed occurrence, a daily series cut by a small maxResults, a read-only calendar, an unknown calendar, bad dates. updateEvent on seeded events, read back with listEvents and in the .ics file Thunderbird wrote: title, dates (timed and all-day, where endDate is the last day), location and description, status (set, case-insensitive, cleared), showAs (busy, free, null clears TRANSP), categories (set and cleared), onlineMeeting on and off, reminders and the warnings for a recurring event; deleteEvent of the whole series. Errors of updateEvent: nothing to change, unknown event, bad dates, an end that is not after the start, a status out of the list, unknown and read-only calendars, no eventId. Not covered: calendars other than ics and storage ones (CalDAV, Exchange), several changed occurrences of one series, createEvent (see calendar-create.json). Nothing is sent.",
